Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.8[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Added the value of affinity[/b] to the suppliers. A mouse-over inside the game explains in detail how it works;
[*] Added more information inside the panel of the owned items. With a mouse-over on the written in the center of the screen you can access to a brief explanation of the numbers;
[*] Updated the engine of the quest system. The internal estimate for quests and rewards is more balanced;
[*] Updated the aspect of the quests, now the result of the quest undertaken is highlighted;
[*] Added a counter on quantity in the purchase activity related to the number of ingredients inside the warehouse;
[*] Major updates to the Sabotages feature (not active yet, we are working to release them soon);
[*] Multiple minor fixes.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you!

Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.7[/b]:
[list]
[*] Major update to the engine related to the Stress;
[*] Updated the algorithm related to stress. Now is less probable to lose activities due to stress. Remember that adding more than two activities per day, without having the correct perks can cause too much stress;
[*] Fixed the Reset button in Shop management in case that a quest with a potion as reward is completed inside the activity;
[*] Fixed the check at the start of the activity to see if there are potions to be transferred;
[*] Fixed the quantity inside the Ring after the tutorial, sometimes the quantity was changing at the end of the tutorial;
[*] A lot of improvements regarding sabotages in few of the release of that feature;
[*] Many minor fixes.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you!

Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.6[/b]:
[list]
[*] The code of the entire purchase phase has been updated. It behaves as before, but now it correctly updates the spaces in the cart and moves the pages correctly by loading all the necessary elements;
[*] Updated the entry and exit system from the tutorial so that it no longer creates bugs;
[*] Fixed a bug on the default name on the potions;
[*] Fixed a bug with the helper not being shown correctly on the right of the ring when active in the activity;
[*] Updated the Stress system. Now is less invasive. Remember that 2 activities are still the optimal number to be placed in each day without the related perks;
[*] Updated the code for the warehouse activity, now it always displays the quantities correctly;
[*] Updated the behavior of the warehouse activity while moving potions, using the reset button and performing quests;
[*] Many minor fixes.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you!

Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.5[/b]:
[list]
[*] Fixed the behavior of the partner when it has been liquidated. You can access the partner panel by clicking the button in the upper right left corner of the alchemist tab;
[*] Fixed a bug which caused the reputation to drop a lot in short time;
[*] Fixed some texts in Italian that were displayed also in the English version;
[*] Updated the behavior of the stress inside the organizer. This update affects also the burnout state (flames icon) that were causing a lot of problems;
[*] Added new type of quests;
[*] Fixed the behavior of the tutorial button in the tools screen;
[*] Enhanced the aspect of some panels;
[*] Updated some mouse hover texts;
[*] Fixed the behavior of multiple pop ups and screens;
[*] Fixed some minor graphical bugs.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you!

Among other things, this update improves the use of quests and client quests. To get the client quests you will have to satisfy him as best as possible. Help could come from having potions with two green labels, low toxicity, high tier, and good packaging.

Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.4[/b]:
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug in the client quests, sometimes when a new client quest appeared, client information was hidden;
[*] Fixed an overlap of panels when some quests appeared;
[*] Fixed the functioning of some quests that previously made some of the texts disappear;
[*] Fixed the bug that incorrectly showed some quest buttons disabled;
[*] Fixed a bug in the selling phase that made buttons to serve the customer invisible;
[*] Added a feedback text when reaching the maximum number of available and not yet completed quests;
[*] The code that manages the quest system has been updated;
[*] Updated the functioning of the quests and their functioning with the client quests.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you!

Here is a list of the bugs fixed with [b]patch 1.1[/b]:
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug in the bulletin board that considered altered states such as stress to be continuous;
[*] Thanks to your feedback, we have improved how stress works. Now there are no more situations in which the system forces you to enter activities that would bring you to be more and more stressed. This caused the flames icon effect that many of you saw on the bulletin board;
[i]The state of burnout (flame icon) occurs when the bulletin board ring is overloaded with activities. To prevent this effect, it is advisable to place a maximum of two activities per working day. We've added a tip regarding this to the loading screen;[/i]
[*] Improved movement of how the burnout/stress updates;
[*] [b]We have planned further improvements to the burnout system. For now the Ring shows if there is a stress peak inside the working week. We want it to be able to show both daily stress spikes and overall stress;[/b]
[*] Loading screen updated. We've included some new tips that may help you better understand some of the game's hidden mechanics. Many other future updates will cover this aspect;
[*] Improved the functioning of the scroll views.
[/list]


We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
[i]If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you![/i]

Here is a list of the bug fixed with [b]patch 1.0[/b]:
[list]
[*] Fixed the error that resulted in the game crashing when quickly clicking the tutorial button returning to the main menu;
[*] Fixed partner being liquidated and leading to a bug on save slots;
[*] Temporarily disabled the possibility of liquidating the partner. It led to some graphics bugs that we are currently fixing. The saves are still valid;
[*] Fixed the bug on Vignette Rockmoss, when opening the in-game panel, the relevant values were not displayed;
[*] Fixed a minor display issue when completing some milestones.
[/list]

We are still working on all the other feedbacks and bugs.
[i]If you have any consideration or you find a bug, please post it here or in the Steam discussions and we will do our best to solve them. Thank you![/i]

We are very happy to let you try the Demo of Alchemy Emporium.

After 5 weeks of play, the Demo will end and you can start over if you wish.

The Alchemy Emporium Demo will be available until February 9th, be sure to play it first, then it will be disabled by Steam!

If you have any feedback or advice, please let us know in the discussion thread (accessible by clicking "Community Hub" from the Steam Store).

Most of the main features of the game are activated in this build, but some have yet to be finished, which is why they will not be available. Inside this Demo we aim to show you the main aspects of the game that have been already tested. You should also expect some values that still need to be balanced.

List of disabled features:
[list]
[*] Bottom bar-related features (fast access to the organizer, warehouse detailed view, quests, book of potions, Alchemist improvement summary, perk summary, economy summary);
[*] Shady deals and advertising;
[*] Resize of the game window;
[*] Loading/Save of the game (as you may have noticed, now the system is loading the files at the start of each activity);
[*] Books to be purchased and resold later for a profit;
[*] Game over loan (you will have the chance to have some money from the partner that needs to be returned with interests).
[/list]

List of upcoming improvements:
[list]
[*] Improved and animated main menu;
[*] Alchemist starting screen with brand new artworks and rename of the campaign;
[*] Improvements at the notes feature;
[*] Since the game is more complex and deep than it may seem, we plan more explanations inside the game;
[*] General improvements to the progression system;
[*] Balancing the costs of the helpers, transformable ingredients and books;
[*] Improvements to the weather and events system;
[*] We haven't spotted major bugs in the resolution management system, but we suggest to play the game in 1920x1080 for now;
[*] Many more "general" improvements.
[/list]

